---
import CookbookShell from './CookbookShell.astro';
---

<CookbookShell title={`Acknowledgments | BiblicalMeal Cookbook`}>
  <section class="cookbook-content px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24">
    <h1 class="font-display text-h1 text-ink">Acknowledgments</h1>

    <div class="prose-bm mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-body text-ink-muted">
      <p>
        This cookbook is built on the work of scholars, archaeologists, and
        biblical researchers whose dedication to understanding the ancient world
        makes recipes like these possible.
      </p>

      <p>
        We are grateful to the scholars whose published research on ancient Near
        Eastern food, agriculture, and cooking provides the foundation for the
        historical claims in this cookbook. Their work in archaeobotany,
        biblical studies, and culinary history has shaped every recipe and every
        evidence note.
      </p>

      <p>
        Special recognition goes to the translators and commentators who have
        carefully wrestled with the meaning of biblical food terms &mdash; from
        the identification of the seven species to the question of what
        &ldquo;bitter herbs&rdquo; might have been on a Passover table three
        thousand years ago.
      </p>

      <p>
        BiblicalMeal is an independent food publication. This cookbook
        represents our commitment to honest, evidence-aware cooking that honours
        both the biblical text and the uncertainty that surrounds much of what
        we know about ancient food.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-8 text-center text-body text-ink-muted">
        Thank you for cooking with us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</CookbookShell>
